WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:02.170
<v Instructor>So now let's talk about AWS Glue.</v>

2
00:00:02.170 --> 00:00:03.760
So it's a managed ETL service

3
00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:06.000
for doing extract, transform and load.

4
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.610
It's very helpful when you want to prepare

5
00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:10.440
and transform data ahead of doing analytics.

6
00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:12.430
It's a fully serverless service

7
00:00:12.430 --> 00:00:13.690
and the way it works is, for example,

8
00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:15.510
you have Glue ETL here

9
00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:17.060
and you have data in an Amazon S3 bucket

10
00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:19.820
that you can extract or an Amazon RDS database

11
00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:21.310
that you can extract as well,

12
00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:24.220
and then you would transform it within Glue ETL,

13
00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:26.840
and finally load it where your target is.

14
00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:29.630
For example, it could be a Redshift data warehouse.

15
00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:31.610
So this is the Glue ETL service

16
00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:34.640
and then you have the Glue Data Catalog service.

17
00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:38.210
So the Glue Data Catalog is a catalog of data sets

18
00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:41.400
and they will just have a crawler out there

19
00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:43.530
that will look into all your data sources possible,

20
00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:47.490
so it could be Amazon S3, Amazon RDS, Amazon DynamoDB,

21
00:00:47.490 --> 00:00:49.620
or any JDBC compatible database,

22
00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:52.920
and the crawler is going to look at these databases,

23
00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:55.220
find all the tables and write the metadata

24
00:00:55.220 --> 00:00:59.740
back into the AWS Data Catalog on AWS Glue.

25
00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:01.350
So we'll have met our databases,

26
00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:04.380
so a bunch of table metadata. Why?

27
00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:06.970
Well, because once we have the data catalog

28
00:01:06.970 --> 00:01:10.130
set in place, then the Glue Jobs ETL

29
00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:12.990
can find these tables, know how to connect to them,

30
00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:15.020
find the columns, find the rows and so on,

31
00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:17.820
and then, for example, other services of AWS

32
00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:20.100
also rely on the Glue Data Catalog.

33
00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:22.400
For example, Amazon Athena is using

34
00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:24.920
the Glue Data Catalog to do data discovery,

35
00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:29.670
Amazon Redshift Spectrum as well, and Amazon EMR.

36
00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:30.503
So that's it for Glue.

37
00:01:30.503 --> 00:01:31.980
You just need to know it at a high level.

38
00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:33.150
Hopefully that's enough

39
00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:35.100
and I will see you in the next lecture.

